; The screens of the game, each drawn by the game's own code: #DRAWSCREEN
; (src/shadskim.ref) runs the screen clear and the screen entry in SkoolKit's
; simulator, and #SCR takes the play area. The hull map tiles the same draws
; through ScreenWriter.hull_map (src/screens.py).

[Page:Screens]
SectionPrefix=Screen

[Screen:hull-map:Hull map]
Every screen of the outer hull, drawn as at #R$D8DC(the outer hull layouts). The
screens sit where #R$CE86(the hull map) puts them, from screen 0 at the top left. The
renders draw each screen as a new game finds it, when every #R$BD40(defence
device) stands.

#HTML(<div style="overflow-x: auto">)#UDGTABLE { #CALL(hull_map(hull_map)) } TABLE##HTML(</div>)

[Screen:outer-hull:Outer hull]
Each screen of the outer hull, linked to its #R$D8DC(layout).

